# Git Workflow

Single entry point for git-related operations. Use the rule that matches the scenario.

## When to use which rule

| Scenario | Rule |
|----------|------|
| Starting a task / creating a branch | `linear-task-branch.mdc` |
| Writing commit messages | `commit-messages.mdc` |
| Creating or updating a PR | `pull-request-template.mdc` |

## Conventions

- **Default branch:** `main`. Use the repo default; confirm in the project if unsure. Do not force-push to the default branch.
- **Branch prefix:** Must be `feat/`, `fix/`, or `chore/` (no username prefix). See `linear-task-branch.mdc`.

## Tooling

Pre-commit runs **lint-staged** (ESLint fix + Prettier format). See `matchvaga-project-overview.mdc` (DX Tooling).
